    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add focus-without-user-activation compatibility data]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30991</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30991"/>
        <updated>2026-10-28T14:00:29.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128292743?u=3e557f09456339e289afa5d06625e4c955e0a4e6&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Adds compatibility data for the <code class="notranslate">focus-without-user-activation</code> Permissions Policy and notes Chromium's different default allowlist. Chrome is recorded as <code class="notranslate">preview</code>: Canary 158.0.8127.2 enabled the feature by default, while Dev 158.0.8117.2 still marked it experimental.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">npm test</code> passed on the contribution branch.</li>
<li><a href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/681cd621e82e606d7536eae8ea2576afb3c7d65c/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5" rel="nofollow">Chrome Canary runtime configuration</a> and <a href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/4f9bd52e089070d5916e47f120f5848c9b04c3f4/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5" rel="nofollow">Dev runtime configuration</a> show the difference.</li>
