        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30979</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30979"/>
        <updated>2026-10-27T09:49:08.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">…rted</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Firefox 159 fixes a bug whereby previously, max<em>In</em>Stage limits (see <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUSupportedLimits" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">GPUSupportedLimits</code></a>) were adjusted to the values of max<em>Per</em>Stage limits, but those adjustments were not correctly reported in the device limits.</p>
<p dir="auto">Those adjustments are now correctly reported. See <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2006720" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2006720</a>, particularly the comments from <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2006720#c26" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2006720#c26</a> onward.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR updates the 151 notes to be more accurate and adds an entry showing the problem was fixed in 159. It's a bit of a weird situation, and hard to understand, and I've tried my best based on the info I've been given.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>

]]></content>
